id=a52sxq_wireless_dex
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Samsung DeX entry points lead to wireless DeX
author=kusti420
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE. One UI 9 DeX is desktop windowing on an external display; on a phone it is started wirelessly by the launcher's ConnectivityActivity (Smart View/Miracast connection with SemWifiDisplayConfig mode 2, which system_server turns into an external desktop display). The framework and WMShell side is the same as on the S26U once desktop windowing is on (sff.sh). But Settings > Connected devices > Samsung DeX and the launcher's DeX quick settings tile only offer it when /sys/class/dp_sec/dex exists, i.e. on a phone with DisplayPort alt mode; the A52s kernel has no CONFIG_SEC_DISPLAYPORT, so the Settings entry is hidden and the tile takes the tablet "DeX on this screen" branch instead of the wireless one. Settings: ExternalDisplayUtils.isWirelessDexOnlyDevice() returns true (wireless-only help text, entry shown). Launcher: its "Supports dp" check returns true, so the tile opens the wireless device list. Nothing changes until DeX is started; wired DeX stays impossible (no DP alt mode).
